  "problem": "If $A={1,2,4,8,16}$ and $B={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16},$ then $B\u2216A=$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $B\u2216A$ is the set of all elements belonging to $B$ but *not* $A.$ Note that the elements $2,4,8,16\\in A$ are also in $B,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\u2216A & =B-A \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16}-{1,2,4,8,16} \\\\  & ={6,10,12,14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
